RESOLUTION OF THE FIRST BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF [COMPANY NAME], CHUSIK HOESA

I. Recitals

WHEREAS the company has been formed as a Chusik Hoesa under the Commercial Act of the Republic of Korea, and the incorporation registration has been completed or will be completed upon the full payment of the duly subscribed share capital;

WHEREAS all issued shares of the company have been fully subscribed and the subscription price has been deposited with a licensed financial institution in the Republic of Korea in accordance with Article 295 of the Commercial Act;

WHEREAS the directors of the company, as elected in the meeting of incorporators and as named in the Articles of Incorporation, constitute a quorum able to transact business pursuant to the company Axios Articles of Incorporation and Article 363 of the Commercial Act;

WHEREAS the board considers it necessary and appropriate to ratify the capital structure, fix the registered office, establish banking authorities, appoint statutory officers, and approve ancillary governance instruments to permit the company to commence its business of internet retail sales through online marketplaces, including Amazon FBA operations, cross-border e-commerce, and related general import and export activities;

II. Resolutions

1. Capital Ratification. The board resolves that [Number] shares of common stock, par value KRW [Par Value] each, have been validly subscribed and paid in full, resulting in paid-in capital of KRW [Capital], and that the bank deposit certificate and any property valuation reports are approved, accepted, and filed in the permanent corporate records.

2. Registered Office. The board resolves that the registered office shall be located at [Full Address], [City/Province], Republic of Korea, and that legal notices, tax communications, regulatory service of process, and statutory correspondence shall be received at such address.

3. Statutory Officers. The board appoints [Name] as Representative Director and Chief Executive Officer, [Name] as Director, and [Name] as Auditor if required under the Commercial Act; each officer is vested with full statutory authority to execute corporate documents under the corporate seal, except that any instrument exceeding KRW [Threshold] shall require the dual signatures of the authorized officer and one additional director.

4. Banking and Treasury. The board approves the opening of deposit and operating accounts at [Bank], the appointment of authorized signatories, the adoption of an electronic banking mandate, and the use of such accounts solely for valid corporate purposes in strict compliance with the anti-money laundering and foreign exchange transaction laws of the Republic of Korea.

5. Seal and Governance. The approved corporate seal shall be registered with the competent authority, the signatory matrix is adopted, and the corporate secretary shall maintain meeting minutes, share registers, and statutory books at the registered office.

6. General Authorization. The Representative Director is authorized to file all statutory notifications, obtain e-commerce seller registrations, complete Amazon FBA seller account verification, and execute all operational documents necessary to lawfully conduct the company business.
